################################################################################
Hyphenation dictionaries of Chromium (fagus-text)
################################################################################

The files `*.hyb.br` in this directory are the hyphenation dictionaries that Chrome uses on
Linux, Windows, ChromeOS and Android, compressed with Brotli: the `.hyb` files of Chromium's
`third_party/hyphenation-patterns/hyb`
(https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/third_party/hyphenation-patterns,
hyphenation-patterns revision 06ce8d348f9145e41e8f52ff9f83470fe3563084, from
https://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/hyphenation-patterns/), which Minikin's
`mk_hyb_file.py` builds from the TeX hyphenation patterns in that directory's `src/`, where the
sources of each dictionary are available. `hyph-<locale>.hyb` is stored as `<locale>.hyb.br`,
unchanged once decompressed.

The dictionaries of Hungarian (hu, MPL 1.1/GPL 2.0/LGPL 2.1), Armenian (hy, LGPL 2.1), Latvian
(lv, LGPL 2.1/GPL 2) and Russian (ru, LGPL 2.1) are not included. The Swedish dictionary (sv)
is under the Mozilla Public License 2.0; its source form is `src/sv/hyph-sv.pat.txt` and
`src/sv/hyph-sv.chr.txt` at the address above.

The licenses of the included dictionaries follow, as Chromium's `LICENSE` file of
hyphenation-patterns lists them, by dictionary.

